<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Cambodia</h1><p class="st-meta">1993 CE – present · capital Phnom Penh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Present-day Cambodia, a constitutional monarchy restored in 1993 after decades of war, dominated in practice by Hun Sen and the Cambodian People's Party.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the UN-supervised elections of May 1993, a constituent assembly adopted a new constitution, and on 24 September 1993 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">Norodom Sihanouk</a> returned to the throne of a restored <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970">Kingdom of Cambodia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-ranariddh">Norodom Ranariddh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hun-sen">Hun Sen</a> became joint prime ministers of a coalition government.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The king reigns as head of state with limited powers; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">Sihanouk</a> abdicated in 2004 in favour of his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihamoni">Norodom Sihamoni</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hun-sen">Hun Sen</a> ousted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-ranariddh">Ranariddh</a> in fighting in 1997 and dominated politics for decades. The last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a> forces surrendered in 1998. Garment exports, tourism to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor">Angkor</a> and Chinese investment drove growth, while the main opposition party was dissolved in 2017.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>The kingdom continues today. In 2023 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hun-sen">Hun Sen</a> handed the premiership to his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hun-manet">Hun Manet</a>, and in 2024 became president of the Senate. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970">Cambodia</a> joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/association-of-southeast-asian-nations">ASEAN</a> in 1999.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-cambodia.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Cambodia" width="320" height="206"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cambodia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1993 CE – present</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Phnom Penh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Norodom Sihanouk, Norodom Sihamoni, Hun Sen</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Khmer</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Cambodia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cambodia, Kampuchea</dd></dl></aside></div>
